{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-11770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(5,5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(5,5),$ we can substitute $x=5$ and $y=5$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {5}^{2} & =4p(5) \\\\ 25 & =20p \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{5}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "02c72d6aa9aa414c46a7b45bf109fc01e3bfd03d807393d717271958bcbf57c5"} {"question" "q-11770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{2}=-3x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-5x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=3x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=5x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=5x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11793" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/assets/9eb2efa6d60dc4bd1d7915900e60be8a891f824799ed6ada8f2753fa71bb01c6.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11793" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(-2,2)$ and passes through the point $(6,10).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-2,2),$ we substitute $h=-2$ and $k=2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(6,10),$ so we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=10$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+2) \\\\ (10-2)^{2} & =4p(6+2) \\\\ 64 & =32p \\\\ p & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+2) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(2)(x+2) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =8(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=2$ is positive." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11793" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "02c72d6aa9aa414c46a7b45bf109fc01e3bfd03d807393d717271958bcbf57c5"} {"question" "q-11793" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11793" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(y+2)^{2}=8(x-2)"] ["math" "(y-2)^{2}=-4(x+2)"] ["math" "(y-2)^{2}=-8(x+2)"] ["math" "(y-2)^{2}=4(x+2)"] ["math" "(y-2)^{2}=8(x+2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11793" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(y-2)^{2}=8(x+2)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(-3,1)$ and passes through the point $(0,5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-3,1),$ we substitute $h=-3$ and $k=1$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(0,5),$ so we can substitute $x=0$ and $y=5$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x+3) \\\\ (5-1)^{2} & =4p(0+3) \\\\ 16 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x+3) \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{4}{3})(x+3) \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =\\frac{16}{3}(x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "02c72d6aa9aa414c46a7b45bf109fc01e3bfd03d807393d717271958bcbf57c5"} {"question" "q-11808" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11808" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{16}{3}(x-1)"] ["math" "(y-1)^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}(x+3)"] ["math" "(y-1)^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}(x+3)"] ["math" "(y-1)^{2}=\\frac{16}{3}(x+3)"] ["math" "(y-1)^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}(x+3)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-11808" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(y-1)^{2}=\\frac{16}{3}(x+3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-2,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-2,-2),$ we can substitute $x=-2$ and $y=-2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-2)^{2} & =4p(-2) \\\\ 4 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "02c72d6aa9aa414c46a7b45bf109fc01e3bfd03d807393d717271958bcbf57c5"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=2y"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-2x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=4x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=-2x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-115649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(2,0)$ and passes through the point $(0,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-115649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(2,0),$ we substitute $h=2$ and $k=0$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(0,-2),$ so we can substitute $x=0$ and $y=-2$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x-2) \\\\ (-2)^{2} & =4p(0-2) \\\\ 4 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x-2) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{2})(x-2) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-2(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-115649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "02c72d6aa9aa414c46a7b45bf109fc01e3bfd03d807393d717271958bcbf57c5"} {"question" "q-115649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7a124e0c75abf2640e8d81893fe22aba9c4fee5822f09b0f77851c0ed8ffda3"} {"question" "q-115649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x-2)^{2}=2y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=2(y-2)"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}(y-2)"]